      "hints": [
        "Substitute $g(x) = ax^2+b$ into $f(x) = 2x+3$.",
        "Compare coefficients of $x^2$ and the constant term with $6x^2 - 21$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Form the composite function $fg(x)$ by substituting $g(x) = ax^2 + b$ into $f(x) = 2x + 3$:\n$$fg(x) = 2(ax^2 + b) + 3 = 2ax^2 + 2b + 3$$",
        "Equate coefficients with the given formula $fg(x) = 6x^2 - 21$:\n$$2a = 6 \\implies a = 3$$\n$$2b + 3 = -21$$",
        "Solve for $b$:\n$$2b = -24 \\implies b = -12$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Functions": "Forms $2(ax^2+b)+3 = 6x^2-21$ (M1). Obtains $a = 3$ (A1). Obtains $b = -12$ (A1)."
