      "hints": [
        "Note that the domain of $f$ is $x \\ge 0$, so $g(x) \\ge 0$ is required for $fg(x)$ to exist.",
        "Solve $3x^2 - 12 \\ge 0$ for $x$.",
        "Since $x \\le q$, deduce the maximum value $q = -2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Recall that the composite function $fg(x)$ is defined only when the range of $g$ lies within the domain of $f$ ($x \\ge 0$):\n$$g(x) \\ge 0 \\implies 3x^2 - 12 \\ge 0$$",
        "Solve the quadratic inequality for $x$:\n$$3x^2 \\ge 12 \\implies x^2 \\ge 4 \\implies x \\le -2 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad x \\ge 2$$",
        "Since the domain of $g$ is given by $x \\le q$, all values of $x \\le q$ must satisfy $x \\le -2$:\n$$q \\le -2 \\implies \\text{Greatest possible value of } q \\text{ is } -2$$"
      ],
