      "hints": [
        "Rearrange $y = 6x^2 - 21$ to make $x$ the subject.",
        "Choose the negative square root since the domain is $x \\le -3$.",
        "The domain of $(fg)^{-1}$ is the range of $fg$ found in part (iii)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = 6x^2 - 21$ and rearrange to isolate $x^2$:\n$$6x^2 = y + 21 \\implies x^2 = \\frac{y + 21}{6}$$",
        "Take the square root, choosing the negative branch because the domain is $x \\le -3$:\n$$x = -\\sqrt{\\frac{y + 21}{6}}$$",
        "Write the inverse function in terms of $x$:\n$$(fg)^{-1}(x) = -\\sqrt{\\frac{x + 21}{6}}$$",
        "State the domain of $(fg)^{-1}(x)$, which equals the range of $fg(x)$ from part (iii):\n$$\\text{Domain: } x \\ge 33$$"
